license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  A paper and release repository on the skew Hadamard matrices of order
  4(343^d+1), d odd, built from three order-18 cyclotomic sign patterns and
  the Paley pattern in the bordered Wallis-Whiteman array (Kline 2026,
  doi:10.5281/zenodo.21783219). Under independent signed permutations of
  rows and columns, every automorphism fixes the border and acts on all
  eight copies of the field by one map x -> a x^(343^j), a an eighteenth
  power; these maps form a group of order d(343^d-1)/18, which is 19 at
  order 1376. A second system of three patterns is given, and both systems
  are proved to work for every prime p = 7 or 31 mod 36 and field size
  p^(3d), d odd. They give at least eight inequivalent skew Hadamard matrices at
  every such order 4(p^(3d)+1); on the characteristic-7 tower, with the
  published character, the arrangements and transposes give exactly sixteen
  classes when 3 does not divide d. No
  such matrix is equivalent to a Kronecker product, a skew doubling, or a
  matrix of the same array with sextic-class patterns. The orders were
  known. Proofs use a four-row invariant, Weil's bound, Kantor's theorem on
  Paley design automorphisms, and exact finite certificates. Novelty is
  bounded to the sources searched.
keywords:
  - Hadamard matrices
  - skew Hadamard matrices
  - automorphism groups
  - Hadamard equivalence
  - cyclotomy
  - Jacobi sums
  - Wallis-Whiteman array
  - Paley design
